errors=[('Perception','overlook the word underlying in sure→true;miss threatening’s full definition'),('Memory','remember hope as identical to uncertainty;recall a high weight as established evidence'),('Interpretation','read subjective sure as factive;read enough as certainty rather than sufficiency'),('Source','copy the target title but not its definition;attribute an annotation to the original graph'),('Selection','choose only high-weight routes;ignore incoming neighbors because the display hides them'),('Confirmation','find only examples where certainty and hope conflict;discard a valid association because its reason fails'),('Availability','reuse the last successful scope warning on every edge;select truth because it is a familiar endpoint'),('Anchoring','freeze the first L4 match despite the L2 input;let the first table layout define relevant variables'),('Motivated reasoning','call every annotation a beneficial mind change;reject harmless source errors to appear rigorous'),('Social pressure','endorse the source because it belongs to the requested system;perform disagreement merely to appear independent'),('False dichotomy','treat source reason as either valid entailment or useless;force certainty into true or false without actor/time scope'),('Scope','contradict P using uncertainty about Q;claim graph-wide improvement from sure-only work'),('Timing','reuse a past certainty statement as present;apply an expired action threshold to a current decision'),('Causation','attribute a changed verdict solely to layout despite added definition;attribute later correct retrieval to a rule never read'),('Definition','define hope as uncertainty to make contradiction automatic;define useful as source-conforming to guarantee success')]
